<title>HUNGARY: INDICATORS - HUNGARY - UPDATED JUNE 18.</title>
<headline>INDICATORS - HUNGARY - UPDATED JUNE 18.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The latest indicators:</p>
<p> GDP (prelim. pct)    1996 +1.0pct (Q4 3.0 yr/yr Q3 +1.0 yr/yr)</p>
<p> CPI (pct)		May +1.3 m/m +17.7 y/y  (Apr +1.4  +18.6)</p>
<p> PPI (pct)		Apr +1.3m/m +20.0yr/yr (March +1.5 +21.8)</p>
<p> Ind. output(pct)     Apr +9.0m/m +11.4yr/yr  (March -8.6 +3.3)</p>
<p> Current account	Jan-March -$477 mln   (Jan-Feb -$498 mln)</p>
<p> NBH trade deficit    Jan-March $402 mln	(Jan-Feb $439mln)</p>
<p> MIT trade deficit    Jan-April $907 mln  (Jan-March $690 mln)*</p>
<p> Gross foreign debt   March $24,442.5 mln   (Feb $24,440.8 mln)</p>
<p> Net foreign debt     March $12,570.3 mln   (Feb $12,754.2 mln)</p>
<p> Unemployment (pct)   May 10.6 pct		 (April 10.8 pct)</p>
<p> Budget balance (HUF) Jan-May -150 bln    (Jan-April -126.7bln)</p>
<p>T-bill yields% (1mo) 20.75 (3mo) 20.26 (6mo) 20.47 (1yr) 20.18</p>
<p>Government bond yields:(2-yr 1999/F) 18.81 (3-yr 2000/E) 17.42</p>
<p>(5-yr 2001/C) 15.82  7-yr bond avg price: (2004/F) 101.67 pct</p>
<p>The NBH is BBB by Duff &amp; Phelps, BBB-minus by S&amp;P, IBCA and</p>
<p>Thomson BankWatch, Baa3 by Moody's Investors Service, BBB+ by</p>
<p>the Japan Credit Rating Agency.</p>
<p>* The National Bank of Hungary's (NBH) March current</p>
<p>account and trade figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>** The January-March and January-April Ministry of Industry</p>
<p>and Trade and Tourism (MIT) trade deficit figures are</p>
<p>preliminary and are likely to be reduced. NBH trade data are</p>
<p>based on cash flow, MIT data on customs statistics.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
